DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ffffss(), ffffssll() and ffffssllll() functions find the first (least signifi‐
     cant) bit set in _v_a_l_u_e and return the index of that bit.

     The ffllss(), ffllssll() and ffllssllll() functions find the last (most significant)
     bit set in _v_a_l_u_e and return the index of that bit.

     Bits are numbered starting at 1, the least significant bit.  A return
     value of zero from any of these functions means that the argument was
     zero.

